meta {
  name: Rubric
  seq: 5
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  The rubric tree of the site. Run in `seq` order:
  
  1. `List rubrics of the site`, `Search rubrics of the site`, `Show a rubric`, `List filter aspects of a rubric` — `rubricId` of the environment.
  2. `Show a brand in a rubric`, `Update texts of a brand in a rubric` — `rubricId` and `brandId` from `Brand / List brands with products on the site`. The update example sets only `meta_robots` to `INDEX, FOLLOW`, the value the storefront uses when none is set: put the texts and a locale of your site.
  3. `Create a rubric` under `rubricId` → `createdRubricId`. `Deactivate a rubric`, `Update a rubric`, `Move a rubric`, `Activate a rubric` and `Delete a rubric` work with `createdRubricId` only, so the rubric of the environment is never changed or deleted. Run `Create a rubric` first: without it these requests have no id.
}
